Q: How can I restrict a method to only classes implementing a specific interface in Java? A: <p>Right now,  <code>heal(int amount)</code> is public in <code>GameCharacter</code>, so <em>any</em> subclass (like <code>Warrior</code>) can call it directly. You want only <code>Healer</code> to be able to trigger healing, while still preserving encapsulation.</p>
<p>Either you can Restrict <code>heal(int amount)</code> to package-private or protected or Separate Healing into a Capability Interface</p>
<pre><code>public interface HealingCapability {
    void receiveHealing(int amount);
}

public abstract class GameCharacter implements HealingCapability {
    private int currentHealth;
    private int maxHealth;

    @Override
    public void receiveHealing(int amount) {
        currentHealth = Math.min(maxHealth, currentHealth + amount);
    }
}

public class Healer extends GameCharacter {
    private final int healingPower = 20;

    public void heal(GameCharacter target) {
        target.receiveHealing(healingPower);
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>now here receiveHealing is part of the internal contract, only Healer expose the action and other characters can receive healing but can not initiate it.</p>

Q: How to replace values of multiple columns with other columns within the same dataframe? A: <p>A <code>R base</code> solution is, using a simple for loop, seq_len and ifelse functions:</p>
<pre><code>k = ncol(test) / 2

for(i in seq_len(k)) {
    test[, i] = ifelse(is.na(test[, i]), test[, k + i], test[, i])
}
</code></pre>

Q: Angular Access inner component of ng-template A: <p>The template <strong>#top</strong> needs to loaded into some container to exist in the DOM and get picked up by <strong>@ViewChild</strong>.
Easiest method is using a simple structural directive.
It the below example <strong>NotReady</strong> is a boolean you set to false after your ngInit has completed.</p>
<pre><code>&lt;div *ngIf=&quot;notReady else top&quot;&gt; 
    loading... 
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ng-template #top&gt;
    &lt;inner-selector #inner&gt;&lt;/inner-selector&gt;
&lt;/ng-template&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Note the @ViewChild('top') will need to be mapped to as <strong>static:false</strong>, as it may not be available/exist until after ngOnInit().
#top is then searched for on each change detection cycle, useful when using conditional directives like *ngIf.</p>
<pre><code>//... imports ...

@Component({
  // selector, styles etc
})
export class TopComponent implements AfterViewInit {

  notReady: boolean = true;

  @ViewChild(&quot;top&quot;, { static: false })  topComp : NgbModal;
  // NgbModal is a type provided by some 3rd-party library
  // I can't modify it

  ngInit(){
    this.notReady = false;
  }

  ngAfterViewInit() {
    // let's access the #inner component from here
  }
}
</code></pre>

Q: How to copy a file from one server to other server which is in different environment? A: <p>You can try this code(you would have to implement Impersonator class <a href="https://www.codeproject.com/Articles/10090/A-small-C-Class-for-impersonating-a-User" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://www.codeproject.com/Articles/10090/A-small-C-Class-for-impersonating-a-User</a>):</p>

<pre><code>using ( new Impersonator( "remoteUsername", "remoteDomain", "remotePassword" ) )
{
   File.Copy("C:\test\copy.txt", "\\anotherMachine\c$\test\copy.txt" );
}
</code></pre>

<p>The code above assumes you got the user that have the required permission.</p>

Q: How to filter a wordpress search by taxonomy terms? A: <p>There is a way to do this, let's say that we have a custom post type called &quot;<em>podcast</em>&quot; which has a custom taxonomy attached to it called &quot;<em>season</em>&quot;. What we want to do is order the &quot;<em>podcast</em>&quot; posts by &quot;<em>season</em>&quot;.</p>
<p>So first of all we need to get all the terms of &quot;<em>season</em>&quot; and order them by name, then we need to loop through the seasons, inside the seasons loop we have to get the podcast posts that belong to the current season and finally loop through them.</p>
<p>Here is the code:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;?php
// get the seasons term
$seasons = get_terms(array(
   'taxonomy'   =&gt; 'season',
   'orderby' =&gt; 'name',
   'order' =&gt; 'DESC',
));

// if $seasons exists loop through seasons
if ($seasons) :
  foreach ($seasons as $season) :

    // query podcasts based on current season
    $args = array(
      'post_type' =&gt; 'podcast',
      'post_status' =&gt; 'publish',
      'posts_per_page' =&gt; -1,
      'orderby' =&gt; 'DATE',
      'tax_query' =&gt; [
        [
          'taxonomy' =&gt; 'season',
          'field' =&gt; 'slug',
          'terms' =&gt; $season-&gt;slug,
        ]
      ],
    );

    $podcasts = new WP_Query($args);

    // loop through the podcasts
    if ($podcasts-&gt;have_posts()) : ?&gt;
      &lt;div class=&quot;podcast-season-wrapper&quot; data-season=&quot;&lt;?= $season-&gt;slug ?&gt;&quot;&gt;
        &lt;h2 class=&quot;podcasts-season-title&quot;&gt;&lt;?= $season-&gt;name ?&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
        &lt;?php
        while ($podcasts-&gt;have_posts()) : $podcasts-&gt;the_post();
          get_template_part('template-partials/posts/podcast-loop', null, ['season' =&gt; $season]);
        endwhile; ?&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;&lt;?php
    endif;
    wp_reset_postdata();
  endforeach;
endif;
</code></pre>
